WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:25.090
We're going to start today talking about John.

00:00:25.090 --> 00:00:30.039
And there is so much to say and so many different
angles to this story.

00:00:30.039 --> 00:00:31.300
So let's get right into it.

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:35.710
One of Donald Trump's former national security
advisers, because he's had many, is very close

00:00:35.710 --> 00:00:37.790
to releasing a book.

00:00:37.790 --> 00:00:41.940
The book is scheduled to be released on Tuesday,
June twenty third.

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:46.520
We have a bunch of the claims that are in
the book to tell you about momentarily.

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:51.340
But the first part of this is about Donald
Trump and the Justice Department under Donald

00:00:51.340 --> 00:00:57.550
Trump's A.G., William Barr working really
hard to suppress the release of the book The

00:00:57.550 --> 00:00:59.100
Eye.

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:00.379
The story needs a disclaimer.

00:01:00.379 --> 00:01:01.460
Now, I want to be.

00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:05.300
I'm going to keep saying this today because
it's important, because it's been a few months

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:08.160
since we last talked about John Bolton's book.

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:10.660
John Bolton is absolutely horrible.

00:01:10.660 --> 00:01:16.330
John Bolton is of the worst of the worst when
it comes to his political worldview.

00:01:16.330 --> 00:01:21.530
He's one of the key architects of the 2003
Iraq war, which doesn't seem he regrets being

00:01:21.530 --> 00:01:22.530
a part of.

00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:25.560
To this day, he's a horrible neoconservative.

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:31.220
He's not someone that progressives would ever
consider an ally on policy and someone whose

00:01:31.220 --> 00:01:34.550
entire moral compass is fundamentally broken.

00:01:34.550 --> 00:01:39.909
So I the reason I want to do this is there
is already some supposed leftists out there

00:01:39.909 --> 00:01:42.800
talking about liberals are falling for Bush.

00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:47.530
They're falling all over themselves to praise
Bolton.

00:01:47.530 --> 00:01:51.970
Bad people sometimes tell the truth, in other
words, that people are always lying.

00:01:51.970 --> 00:01:59.061
John Bolton seems to be a fierce advocate
for what he believes is right and true, and

00:01:59.061 --> 00:02:01.510
he doesn't tend to get pushed around.

00:02:01.510 --> 00:02:08.899
I almost always disagree with him about what
is right in this particular case.

00:02:08.899 --> 00:02:13.920
Bolton has decided that it is correct and
profitable and this is important.

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:18.010
We're going to get into that to tell the story,
as he sees it, of what happened when he was

00:02:18.010 --> 00:02:20.739
Donald Trump's national security adviser.

00:02:20.739 --> 00:02:23.210
This is not praise of John Bolton.

00:02:23.210 --> 00:02:24.600
And I'm going to go back to that.

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:30.080
So the Trump administration has been panicking
and they have sued Bolton to try to prevent

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:31.810
the release of the book.

00:02:31.810 --> 00:02:35.160
Trump's Justice Department is trying to suppress
the book.

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:36.160
Remember this?

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:38.580
They said this would be the most transparent
administration ever.

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:41.639
The most for free speech administration ever.

00:02:41.639 --> 00:02:46.750
They're going through any number of different
arguments, trying anything they can to see

00:02:46.750 --> 00:02:52.269
what sticks, including claiming that the publication
of Bolton's book risks compromising national

00:02:52.269 --> 00:02:53.269
security.

00:02:53.269 --> 00:03:00.150
Now, there is something funny in that there
is some truth in the national security concerns

00:03:00.150 --> 00:03:01.240
around Bolton's book.

00:03:01.240 --> 00:03:07.940
But what I mean by that is what Bolton alleges
in the book, which I will get to, is so damning

00:03:07.940 --> 00:03:14.090
to Donald Trump that it exposes the United
States to being taken advantage, advantage

00:03:14.090 --> 00:03:18.959
of by showing how incompetent and clueless
Donald Trump is.

00:03:18.959 --> 00:03:24.040
It actually might encourage our adversaries
to try to take advantage of the United States

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:28.830
knowing how incompetent Donald Trump is, according
to the book.

00:03:28.830 --> 00:03:33.180
But from a legal perspective, these arguments
are all very tired.

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:34.620
They're likely not going to work.

00:03:34.620 --> 00:03:38.590
Partially thanks to the First Amendment, to
the Constitution of the United States.

00:03:38.590 --> 00:03:42.329
Now, in the lawsuit against Bolton, there's
a few different arguments.

00:03:42.329 --> 00:03:47.640
The lawsuit says Bolton violated the contract
he signed when he became national security

00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:49.709
adviser by writing the book.

00:03:49.709 --> 00:03:54.359
They make another argument in the lawsuit
that says Bolton has not allowed enough time

00:03:54.359 --> 00:03:58.919
for the book to be vetted to see if it contains
government secrets.

00:03:58.919 --> 00:04:03.859
Donald Trump the other day said he thinks
if the book gets published, Bolton will have

00:04:03.859 --> 00:04:05.780
criminal problems.

00:04:05.780 --> 00:04:11.370
But before we get into that, here is Trump
saying any conversation with him is de facto

00:04:11.370 --> 00:04:15.290
classified, which is another argument he's
making about why Bolton's book shouldn't be

00:04:15.290 --> 00:04:16.290
published.

00:04:16.290 --> 00:04:17.850
And somebody said he went out and wrote a
book.

00:04:17.850 --> 00:04:18.850
He wrote a book.

00:04:18.850 --> 00:04:24.270
I can't imagine that he can because that's
highly classified information, even conversations

00:04:24.270 --> 00:04:25.770
with me.

00:04:25.770 --> 00:04:26.850
They're highly classified.

00:04:26.850 --> 00:04:28.770
I told that to the attorney general before.

00:04:28.770 --> 00:04:32.270
I will consider every conversation with me
as president.

00:04:32.270 --> 00:04:33.270
Highly classified.

00:04:33.270 --> 00:04:34.770
Now, that isn't true.

00:04:34.770 --> 00:04:38.729
Presidents can choose to classify or declassify
whatever they want.

00:04:38.729 --> 00:04:43.289
But there is no legal basis to say retroactively.

00:04:43.289 --> 00:04:46.259
Every conversation that I had with Bolton
is classified.

00:04:46.259 --> 00:04:48.830
That's an insanely broad legal claim.

00:04:48.830 --> 00:04:52.090
Courts are very unlikely to accept such a
claim.

00:04:52.090 --> 00:04:53.090
Let's keep going, though.

00:04:53.090 --> 00:04:56.430
Here's more of what Trump said about Bolton
being a criminal.

00:04:56.430 --> 00:05:00.439
So that would mean that if he wrote a book
and if the book gets out, he's broken the

00:05:00.439 --> 00:05:01.439
law.

00:05:01.439 --> 00:05:03.020
And I would think that he would have criminal
problems.

00:05:03.020 --> 00:05:04.020
I hope so.

00:05:04.020 --> 00:05:09.319
Otherwise, I mean, they put a seller in jail
because he sent a photograph of his bed and

00:05:09.319 --> 00:05:11.389
an engine of an old submarine.

00:05:11.389 --> 00:05:17.720
And this guy's writing writing things about
conversations or about anything.

00:05:17.720 --> 00:05:19.120
And maybe he's not telling the truth.

00:05:19.120 --> 00:05:21.860
He's been known not to tell the truth a lot.

00:05:21.860 --> 00:05:26.919
So legal experts believe that Bolton would
not have legal problems, but his publisher

00:05:26.919 --> 00:05:30.020
would also potentially be liable there.

00:05:30.020 --> 00:05:34.949
And the publisher has obviously done a huge
legal review before the book is going to print.

00:05:34.949 --> 00:05:37.780
The First Amendment is quite strong here as
well.

00:05:37.780 --> 00:05:43.400
Now, there is a footnote in the lawsuit against
Bolton where the Department of Justice is

00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:49.969
asking a court to ban every bookstore in the
United States from selling the book.

00:05:49.969 --> 00:05:52.199
That is critical of President Trump.

00:05:52.199 --> 00:05:59.069
What would we be saying if in any other country
we saw a court being asked by a president

00:05:59.069 --> 00:06:03.099
to ban bookstores from selling a book that's
critical of the president?

00:06:03.099 --> 00:06:04.099
Just think about that.

00:06:04.099 --> 00:06:09.320
And when we see all of these supposedly enlightened
hot takes from some on the left saying, oh,

00:06:09.320 --> 00:06:17.590
it's liberals falling for it again now believing
Bolton, who in 2003 was the bad guy.

00:06:17.590 --> 00:06:25.199
What would we be saying if a different country
was trying to use the courts to prevent bookstores

00:06:25.199 --> 00:06:26.509
from publishing a book?

00:06:26.509 --> 00:06:31.210
Now, the reality in terms of the vetting is
that the manuscript was first sent to the

00:06:31.210 --> 00:06:34.800
White House's National Security Council in
December.

00:06:34.800 --> 00:06:36.270
That's six, seven months ago.

00:06:36.270 --> 00:06:37.569
At this point.

00:06:37.569 --> 00:06:40.849
And ultimately, this is not about classified
information.

00:06:40.849 --> 00:06:42.249
This is not about state secrets.

00:06:42.249 --> 00:06:44.770
This is not really about national security.

00:06:44.770 --> 00:06:50.150
This is about a book whose claims and content
is very embarrassing to Donald Trump.

00:06:50.150 --> 00:06:51.550
That's really what this is about.

00:06:51.550 --> 00:06:57.910
Now, I have to tell you, Trump's concern may
be overblown to a degree, because, yes, now

00:06:57.910 --> 00:07:01.659
that we found out what's in the book, which
I'll tell you in a moment, a lot of media

00:07:01.659 --> 00:07:03.840
coverage of it.

00:07:03.840 --> 00:07:08.409
But most Trump lists aren't going to buy and
read a book with several hundred pages that

00:07:08.409 --> 00:07:10.780
that that's not what Trump has to do.

00:07:10.780 --> 00:07:17.279
Most Trump lists are going to see what Fox
News and Bright Bart and OJ N and, you know,

00:07:17.279 --> 00:07:20.330
Mark Levin say about the book.

00:07:20.330 --> 00:07:21.669
And that will be what they believe.

00:07:21.669 --> 00:07:28.259
So I think some of the concern may be overblown,
but what we've learned so far is that Donald

00:07:28.259 --> 00:07:31.639
Trump is focused solely on reelection.

00:07:31.639 --> 00:07:36.539
And to the extent that he believes the book
may hurt his reelection, he's going to do

00:07:36.539 --> 00:07:39.110
everything he can to suppress the book.

00:07:39.110 --> 00:07:42.960
Now, we're going to talk more about skepticism
in a moment.

00:07:42.960 --> 00:07:48.849
We should apply skepticism here to John Bolton,
as we always should.

00:07:48.849 --> 00:07:54.509
When there is a book, because John Bolton
is going to make money from this book.

00:07:54.509 --> 00:07:59.210
If John Bolton's only priority was to get
the truth out, he could have been doing interviews

00:07:59.210 --> 00:08:01.080
seven months ago and telling us what's in
the book.

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:06.220
I'm going to argue later on in the show that
John Bolton is actually a traitor to the United

00:08:06.220 --> 00:08:13.389
States for waiting seven months to tell us
about such damning allegations against Donald

00:08:13.389 --> 00:08:14.389
Trump.

00:08:14.389 --> 00:08:18.939
So there is no doubt that there is a financial
calculation here for John Bolton that doesn't

00:08:18.939 --> 00:08:23.550
tell us whether the claims in the book are
true or false.

00:08:23.550 --> 00:08:27.970
And we have to see if the claims pass the
sniff test.

00:08:27.970 --> 00:08:28.970
And they do.

00:08:28.970 --> 00:08:32.440
We have to see if the claims are similar to
those that have been made by others who have

00:08:32.440 --> 00:08:34.770
spent time around around Donald Trump.

00:08:34.770 --> 00:08:35.770
And they are.

00:08:35.770 --> 00:08:41.229
So is John Bolton hypocritical in the sense
that he didn't testify for the House impeachment

00:08:41.229 --> 00:08:47.170
trial and now he's publishing a book to make
money with absolutely bombshell claims when

00:08:47.170 --> 00:08:49.310
he could have told us about these seven months
ago?

00:08:49.310 --> 00:08:50.310
Absolutely.

00:08:50.310 --> 00:08:53.220
And I'm going to slam him for it in about
15 minutes.

00:08:53.220 --> 00:08:58.750
But that doesn't mean that the claims are
untrue and that is what we are going to be

00:08:58.750 --> 00:08:59.800
talking about.

00:08:59.800 --> 00:09:04.160
Again, I don't know that this is really going
to change Trump's standing with Trump ists

00:09:04.160 --> 00:09:05.500
who aren't really going to read the book.

00:09:05.500 --> 00:09:09.100
They don't really read, but every little bit.

00:09:09.100 --> 00:09:13.340
Anything that can help us remove Donald Trump
in November is something that we should be

00:09:13.340 --> 00:09:15.440
looking at very, very, very seriously.

00:09:15.440 --> 00:09:16.170
And that's exactly what we're going to do
next

